# Design System foundation

{{PROJECT_NAME}} builds all product UI from a small set of documented, tested, token-driven
**design-system primitives**. This rulebook uses the prefix `ds` in examples
(`dsButton`, `dsPanel`); pick one short prefix for your project and use it everywhere.

## Contract

Every new screen, modal, panel, list, and form composes design-system primitives:

1. Find the matching primitive in the design-system documentation.
2. If it does not exist → **create the primitive package first** (folder, `index.ts`,
   component file, `styled.ts`, stories, rules, tests, doc page).
3. Only then build the consuming screen.

**Never** build bespoke screen UI intending to "promote it to the design system later."
That promotion never happens; the debt compounds.

## Naming and package layout

- Prefix every primitive with the chosen design-system prefix; folder:
  `src/components/dsComponentName/`.
- Single-component package:

```
dsComponentName/
├── index.ts                     # barrel
├── dsComponentName.tsx          # markup and wiring only
├── styled.ts                    # all style declarations
├── dsComponentName.stories.tsx  # Storybook coverage
├── <helper>Rules.ts             # extractable pure logic (optional)
└── <helper>Rules.test.ts
```

- **Bounded multi-component packages** are allowed when several primitives share one
  concern (e.g. a form family): several component files with shared rules in one folder
  behind a single `index.ts` barrel.

## Platform divergence inside primitives

Same public API on iOS, Android, and Web:

- **Value-level:** `Platform.select` at the smallest scope.
- **Implementation-level:** `.web.tsx` / `.web.ts` sibling with identical exports; shared
  logic in a platform-neutral `*Rules.ts`.
- Split into a `.web.tsx` when more than 2–3 web branches accumulate.
- Both variants are exercised in native and web Storybook.

## Layer ownership (quick reference)

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Surface / card | panel primitive |
| Action | button / icon-button primitive |
| Read-only text | typography primitive with variant tokens |
| Editable text | text-input primitive |
| Page shell | page-layout primitive (padding, safe area, keyboard) |
| Modal | modal provider + modal-layout primitive |
| Toast / feedback | global toast host via its hook |
| Navigation chrome | header and bottom-bar primitives |

## Legacy policy

Components that pre-date the design-system foundation are migrated incrementally. New code
never introduces more legacy: no legacy typography helpers, no third-party UI kits for new
product surfaces, no wrapping children in raw loaders when the button primitive has a
loading state.
